# In the data part of a callable a record whose head is an ordinary Structure is a declaration (the role data, R22,
# item 1): `S()` declares one more, empty occurrence of S and calls nothing, so the bare name S answers nothing (3).
# In root/self code such a record also launches its resolved head; the root
# variant struct_root_declares checks its common argument-shape refusal.
# The declarations of ordinary Structures live in the data part of main; the root holds places and the call main().
sub: main () (
    S(int: k 1)
    S()
    int: seen 0
)
    seen := S\k
main()
int: seen main\data\seen
